 ('048430c8f6acbc893bf5faf8ae819a17a05776b800ff9cc8bd1045940b2d2440',
  'M1. In this next to the last section, we will be talking about donations of time and money\n'
  'to charitable organizations.\n'
  'Charitable organizations include religious or non-profit organizations that help those in\n'
  'need or that serve and support the public interest. They range in size from national\n'
  'organizations like the United Way and the American Red Cross down to local community\n'
  'organizations. They serve a variety of purposes such as religious activity, helping\n'
  'people in need, health care and medical research, education, arts, environment, and\n'
  'international aid. Our definition of charity does not include political contributions.\n'
  'Donations include any gifts of money, assets, or property/goods made directly to the\n'
  'organization, through payroll deduction, or collected by other means on behalf of the\n'
  'charity. This interview is limited to donations made during the calendar year 2006, with\n'
  'one exception. We will be asking you separately about all donations that you made to help\n'
  "victims of last December's tsunami later in this section.\n"
  'During the year 2006, did (you/you or anyone in your family) donate money, assets, or\n'
  'property/goods with a combined value of more than $25 to religious or charitable\n'
  'organizations?',
  'nominal_year_token',
  879,
  883,
  'year',
  None,
  'explicit_no_whole_domain_denotation',
  'first_question_coordinate_frequency_or_comparison_input',
  2007,
  'ER40620'),
