 ('86b3eac01e57b3685d98bd636aa769213f95ee0d88e25b63db4e2d8e81d97fb4',
  'M1. Next, we will be talking about money donations to charitable organizations.\n'
  'Charitable organizations include religious or non-profit organizations that help those in\n'
  'need or that serve and support the public interest. They range in size from national\n'
  'organizations like the United Way and the American Red Cross down to local community\n'
  'organizations. They serve a variety of purposes such as religious activity, helping people\n'
  'in need, health care and medical research, education, arts, environment, and international\n'
  'aid. Our definition of charity does not include political contributions.\n'
  'Donations include any gifts of money, assets, or property or goods made directly to the\n'
  'organization, through payroll deduction, or collected by other means on behalf of the\n'
  'charity. This interview is limited to donations made during the calendar year 2010.\n'
  'During the year 2010, did (you/you or anyone in your family) donate money, assets, or\n'
  'property or goods, with a combined value of more than $25 to religious or charitable\n'
  'organizations?',
  'nominal_year_token',
  842,
  846,
  'year',
  None,
  'explicit_no_whole_domain_denotation',
  'first_question_coordinate_frequency_or_comparison_input',
  2011,
  'ER51959'),
